🚽 Test case: issue #389 review -- a native's opaque pointer result passed
🚽 to a typed user-defined pointer parameter.
🚽
🚽 STDROT_PTR erases its base type by contract (stdrot_api.h), so the
🚽 width-aware pointer-argument check has nothing to compare but the
🚽 level, and treats it like C's `void *`. An earlier revision refused
🚽 `first(test_ptr_source())` ("cannot determine what this pointer points
🚽 to") while accepting `rizz *p = test_ptr_source(); first(p);` -- the
🚽 same pointer, the same information -- so the rule depended on spelling.
🚽 Both spellings are accepted now, and both write the same static int.
🚽
🚽 Needs tests/stdrot/testptr.c, so it is in WASM_PRODUCTION_SKIP
🚽 (tests/run_wasm_tests.mjs).

skibidi set_first(rizz *p, rizz v) {
    p[0] = v;
}

rizz first(rizz *p) {
    bussin p[0];
}

skibidi main {
    set_first(test_ptr_source(), 41);
    rizz *p = test_ptr_source();
    yapping("inline: %d", first(test_ptr_source()));
    set_first(p, 42);
    yapping("stored: %d", first(p));
    bussin 0;
}
